# Manual API requests for the REST Client VS Code extension (humao.rest-client).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Upload a document. To upload every sample at once, run `npm run samples:upload` instead. To try another sample (see samples/README.md), change the `<` path and the part's Content-Type:
#   ../../samples/employment-contract.pdf          application/pdf
#   ../../samples/employment-contract-signed.pdf   application/pdf
#   ../../samples/heating-invoice-scan.pdf         application/pdf
#   ../../samples/cafe-receipt.jpg                 image/jpeg
#   ../../samples/tenancy-agreement.pdf            application/pdf
#   ../../samples/deposit-receipt.jpg              image/jpeg
# The same file twice answers 409 DUPLICATE_DOCUMENT; delete the first one to upload it again.
# @name upload
POST {{baseUrl}}/documents
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ../../samples/employment-contract.pdf
--boundary--

### List documents, newest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/documents

### Get the document from the last upload request; its `status` is pending, processing, done or failed, and `document_type`, `title` and `summary` are null until the worker has classified it
GET {{baseUrl}}/documents/{{upload.response.body.$.id}}

### Get the text of the document from the last upload request, one entry per page; empty while the document is pending or processing, and if it failed
GET {{baseUrl}}/documents/{{upload.response.body.$.id}}/pages

### Delete the document from the last upload request, with its pages and stored file; answers 204 with no body
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/documents/{{upload.response.body.$.id}}

### Ask a question (how it works: README). Upload every sample first, and wait until they are `done`.
# Expect: the tenancy agreement only, though the employment contract also has a notice period; two months, citing page 2
POST {{baseUrl}}/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "How much notice do I need to give my landlord?" }

### Expect: the employment contract and the tenancy agreement; the question fits both
POST {{baseUrl}}/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "What is my notice period?" }

### Expect: the deposit receipt and the tenancy agreement, not the café receipt
POST {{baseUrl}}/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "How much was my deposit?" }

### Expect: the heating invoice, which is in German, answered in English
POST {{baseUrl}}/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "How much did the heating maintenance cost?" }

### Expect: no documents and a null answer; no document is about this
POST {{baseUrl}}/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "What is my passport number?" }

### Get a document that does not exist, to see an error response
GET {{baseUrl}}/documents/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000
